    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361-a3">

                <pb facs="0657" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg557"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Appendix B to No. 347.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Pew to Mr.
                            Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Gloucester, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 7,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We herewith send to your Department our
                    claim for loss sustained by us through the destruction of the seines of the
                    American fishing schooners Ontario and New England belonging tons.</p>
                <p>The particulars are fully set forth in said claim and the affidavits of the
                    masters and crews of said schooners.</p>
                <p>We earnestly hope that the Government of the United States will take such action
                    in the premises as will secure to American vessel-owners, their masters and
                    crews, the right to fish in British waters, granted them by the treaties of
                    Great Britain with the United States. It is a matter of great importance to the
                    fishing interest of New England, and especially to the people of Gloucester. We
                    are not safe in sending vessels to fish in British waters, and, therefore, the
                    rights granted to our people by the Washington treaty are of little value, while
                    the rights granted by the United States to the subjects of Great Britain to
                    bring fish to our markets free of duty is a great damage to our fisheries and of
                    great value to the people of the British provinces.</p>
                <p>With the fullest confidence that our application will receive due
                    consideration,</p>
                <p>We are, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN PEW &amp; SON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—We also inclose you two printed copies of our petition and accompanying
                        affidavits, thinking they may be a convenience to you.—J. P. &amp; S.</p>
                </postscript>







